;; Regulatory source register for JPN-CAO cross-ministerial compliance
;; navigation -- the Cabinet Office coordinated programmes this repository is
;; about, and the statutes they run on.
;;
;; README.md says: every regulatory claim must cite the official CAO source.
;; docs/business-model.md routes a legal conclusion the governor has not
;; cleared to human sign-off.
;;
;; Until this file existed there was no such source. The documents required a
;; citation against a set that did not exist, so nothing in this repository
;; could tell a real citation from an invented one. This is that set.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A regulation not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id, a
;; law id, or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb --classpath scripts scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which
;; re-fetches every entry from the live authority. Each entry carries a
;; :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it. The checks are NOT
;; interchangeable, and the reasons are the main thing this file has to teach.
;;
;; Everything below was measured against these hosts on 2026-08-27. The
;; sibling registers in this cohort are written against other agencies and
;; their host notes DO NOT transfer.
;;
;; -- THIS REPOSITORY'S SUBJECT IS SPLIT ACROSS THREE PAGE HOSTS
;;
;; Not thoroughness -- forced. The Cabinet Office serves the two programmes
;; this repository navigates from two different sites, and neither is the one
;; its own front page is on:
;;
;;   www.cao.go.jp     the ministry proper (organisation, bills, addresses)
;;   www8.cao.go.jp    規制改革 -- the regulatory-reform machinery and the
;;                     所管省庁 proposal-and-answer channel
;;   www.chisou.go.jp  地方創生推進事務局 -- 国家戦略特区 and the special-zone
;;                     proposal route to 主務官庁
;;
;; A register written against one of them is silently missing two thirds of
;; the repository's subject, and the three do not answer a missing page alike.
;;
;; -- www.cao.go.jp AND www8.cao.go.jp SERVE THE SAME 404 AND DIFFER ANYWAY
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27. Both answer a fabricated path with status 404 and a
;; body of 5452 bytes whose sha256 begins d807a1126cf0 -- byte for byte the
;; same document, same title. They are not the same host:
;;
;;                             HEAD Content-Length     GET
;;   www.cao.go.jp   404       (absent)                5452 B
;;   www.cao.go.jp   front     (absent)                15720 B
;;   www8.cao.go.jp  404       5452                    5452 B
;;   www8.cao.go.jp  front     11494                   11494 B
;;
;; www8 reports an accurate Content-Length on HEAD for both. www sends none at
;; all, for either. So a liveness check built on HEAD works on one of these
;; two hosts and cannot distinguish anything on the other -- while both serve
;; an identical 404 body that would make the two look interchangeable. Every
;; check below issues a GET and reads the body.
;;
;; -- www.chisou.go.jp DOES NOT ANSWER 404. IT REDIRECTS.
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;   GET /zzz-no-such-page-9f3c2a1b8e/
;;     302, content-type application/xml, content-length 0,
;;     location /zzz-no-such-page-9f3c2a1b8e/index.html
;;   ...which then answers 404 with 2508 bytes of HTML.
;;
;; A client that does not follow redirects sees a 302 and an empty body: not a
;; live page, not a recognisable missing one, and nothing that says which.
;; This is why scripts/host_probe.cljs sets redirect follow explicitly and
;; documents it as required rather than incidental. One entry below holds the
;; unfollowed 302 live so the claim cannot quietly stop being true.
;;
;; The same redirect answers a missing DOCUMENT: a fabricated .xlsx path comes
;; back 404 text/html, 2508 bytes, first bytes EF BB BF 3C -- a UTF-8 BOM and
;; then a tag. A form check that reads content-type alone would call that an
;; Excel file that failed to parse; one that reads only status would be right
;; here and wrong on a host that soft-404s. Both are checked, plus magic bytes.
;;
;; -- 地方創生 IS ON THE chisou 404 AND CANNOT BE A NEEDLE THERE
;;
;; Occurrences on each fetched 404 body, tags, scripts, styles and comments
;; removed, measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;                        www / www8 404     chisou 404
;;   内閣府                    5                 0
;;   地方創生                   0                 1
;;   規制改革                   0                 0
;;   規制改革推進会議               0                 0
;;   国家戦略特別区域               0                 0
;;   国家戦略特区                 0                 0
;;   特区                     0                 0
;;   提案                     0                 0
;;   所管省庁                   0                 0
;;   総合調整                   0                 0
;;   地域再生                   0                 0
;;   規制のサンドボックス             0                 0
;;
;; 内閣府 is the name of the agency this repository is about and it is on the
;; CAO 404 five times. 地方創生 is the name of the programme office that
;; serves 国家戦略特区 and it is on the chisou 404. Both are the first phrase
;; anyone would reach for; both verify against a page that does not exist.
;;
;; The set is not guessable from how central a term feels -- it is a property
;; of each host's chrome, and the two chromes are different. Needles here are
;; therefore chosen by SUBTRACTING the live 404 body of THAT page's own host,
;; and the verifier redoes that subtraction on every run against the right
;; probe: a needle found on the fetched 404 REFUSES rather than passes.
;;
;; -- SIZE CANNOT IDENTIFY A DOCUMENT ON THESE HOSTS EITHER
;;
;; Every page this register cites, in characters, against its own host's 404
;; (592 for www and www8, 148 for chisou), measured 2026-08-27:
;;
;;    307   p_index.html (実施計画・答申・意見書等)   285 SHORTER than its 404
;;    413   kokusentoc/index.html                  +265
;;    692   houan/index.html                       +100
;;    773   kisei-kaikaku/index.html               +181
;;    964   toc/document.html                      +816
;;    979   about/pmf_index.html                   +387
;;   1206   p_plan.html                            +614
;;   1357   kokkasenryakutoc.html                  +1209
;;   2025   about/address.html                     +1433
;;   2270   hotline/h_index.html                   +1678
;;   2427   kokusentoc/teian.html                  +2279
;;   9220   toc/index.html                         +9072
;;  40384   kisei/meeting/meeting.html             +39792
;;
;; The regulatory-reform publications index is a real, current, load-bearing
;; page and it is SHORTER than the missing page on its own host. A
;; did-I-get-a-substantial-body heuristic passes the 404 and doubts it.
;;
;; Nothing below asserts a size. The landing pages carry dated news items --
;; kisei-kaikaku/index.html was listing 令和８年７月24日 when this was written
;; -- so their length moves while the thing this register cites them for does
;; not. Needles are the pages' own durable headings, never their news items.
;;
;; -- THE MEASURING INSTRUMENT WAS WRONG BEFORE IT WAS RIGHT
;;
;; The first pass of this file was measured with a de-tag ported unchanged
;; from this cohort's MHLW register, and it did not remove <style> or <script>
;; contents. The reason is in scripts/host_probe.cljs and it is worth knowing
;; before trusting any character count in this workspace: in ClojureScript,
;; clojure.string/replace rebuilds the regex it was handed and carries over
;; only the g, i, m and u flags. The s flag -- dotAll -- is DROPPED. So
;; #"(?is)<style.*?</style>" strips a one-line style element, strips an
;; upper-case one, and silently fails on every multi-line one, which is all of
;; them. The stylesheet stays in the document, the next rule strips its angle
;; brackets but not its text, and CSS is counted as page text.
;;
;; On chisou's 404 that was 682 characters measured against 148 measured
;; correctly: nearly three quarters of what a needle would have been
;; subtracted from was stylesheet. A needle like container or margin would
;; have been reported as appearing on the missing page.
;;
;; So there is one instrument, in scripts/host_probe.cljs, built with explicit
;; js/RegExp flags. Every number above is regenerated by
;;   nbb --classpath scripts scripts/measure-host.cljs
;; which calls the same de-tag that verify-facts.cljs subtracts needles with.
;; If you change de-tag, rerun measure-host and update these numbers.
;;
;; -- THE STATUTE HOST IS SHARED WITH THE COHORT AND ITS TRAPS ARE ITS OWN
;;
;; laws.e-gov.go.jp is the same authority the sibling registers use, and the
;; corpus figures were re-counted here rather than copied. Over all 9550 laws,
;; measured 2026-08-27. The law corpus has since grown: the listing endpoint
;; reports total_count 9551 (measured 2026-09-08 while landing this register).
;; :host/corpus-size below carries the LIVE count the verifier enforces; the
;; 2026-08-27 token frequencies in this header were NOT re-tallied over 9551,
;; and are recorded as the 9550-corpus measurement they are.
;;
;;   repeal_status            None 8993, Repeal 414, LossOfEffectiveness 105,
;;                            Expire 38
;;   current_revision_status  CurrentEnforced 8869, Repeal 557,
;;                            PreviousEnforced 110, UnEnforced 14
;;   remain_in_force true     14, of which NOT repealed: 0
;;
;; The last line is the whole reason remain_in_force is never read as an
;; in-force signal: it is true only on law that is already dead. This
;; repository's nearest miss is one of those 14 and it has a control below.

[;; -- HOSTS ----------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; Declared per host because they do not behave alike, and a check written
 ;; against one is wrong about the others. Measured at run time, not read off
 ;; this register.

